From: acww-3ds <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Switch: the build (configure_host.py --os switch) and the host blocks allocated at start-up

configure_host.py --os switch builds the console port (ENHANCED_PORT) for the Nintendo Switch with devkitPro's
devkitA64, libnx and the portlibs' SDL2 (the SDL frontend, the CPU renderers): build_host_switch.ninja,
build/hostswitch_<v>/acww.nro, with nacptool's title and libnx's default icon. The platform layer
(modern/host/plat_switch.c) and the GPU interface's file (gpu3d/gpu3d_gl.c) are the port repository's own files.

include/host_mem.h: on the Switch too the blocks aligned more than a page (DTCM, ITCM, main RAM, the VRAM banks) are
allocated at start-up (HOST_MEM_RUNTIME_ALIGN, as on Windows and macOS). With the 2 MB aligned main RAM block, .bss
started after a gap of 316 KB, and Eden mapped the module about that much short: fopen jumped to address 0, libnx's
devoptab devices lay past the mapping. That its loader sizes the bss from the module's __bss_start__ is inferred from
the sizes, not read in its source; the console's loader is unchecked. The game's units get -D__SWITCH__ for it.
---
 include/host_mem.h      |  5 +--
 tools/configure_host.py | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/host_mem.h b/include/host_mem.h
index 93c020c..c7c5781 100644
--- a/include/host_mem.h
+++ b/include/host_mem.h
@@ -77,8 +77,9 @@ extern HostSysWork gHostSysWork;
 // HOST_MEM_RUNTIME_ALIGN (Windows, macOS): COFF objects can't ask for more than 8 KB of alignment, Mach-O ones for
 // more than 32 KB, so the blocks aligned more (DTCM, ITCM, the main RAM block; vram.c's banks and windows) are
 // allocated at start-up (HostMem_Init, from main.c's early_init) and their names stand for the allocations (sizeof
-// still gives the block's size)
-#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__)
+// still gives the block's size). The Switch too: with a 2 MB aligned .bss, Eden left the bss's last part unmapped
+// (about the gap before it: 2026-11-18)
+#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__SWITCH__)
 #define HOST_MEM_RUNTIME_ALIGN 1
 #else
 #define HOST_MEM_RUNTIME_ALIGN 0
